tuxamp (0.1.0~alpha) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First release of TuxAmp, a Winamp 2.x-style music player for Linux:
    main window, 10-band equalizer and playlist editor, smoothly zoomable
    together by dragging the bottom-right corner.
  * TuxDrop: a full-screen, music-reactive visualizer with 9 presets, beat
    detection and automatic preset cycling.
  * Cast to smart devices on the local network: Chromecast / Google Cast
    (Chromecast, Google and Nest speakers, Android TV) and DLNA renderers
    (smart TVs, Sonos, Kodi), with the EQ applied to the cast audio.
  * Icons: Tux the penguin holding a lightning bolt.
  * Startup voice: "TuxAmp, it really whips the penguin's ass!"
  * See BUGFIXES.md for the bugs fixed during development.

